{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`sweep (windows)` in `.github/workflows/test.yml` is an advisory job (`continue-on-error: true`) whose stated purpose is to make Windows path, temporary-directory, Git and file-lock regressions visible. It has been red at a scale that destroys that signal: run 35250748887 (2026-09-17) reported 1626 failed + 1382 errors. A new Windows regression is indistinguishable from the standing noise.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-16 on the 5 scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (43715434886, 43748511894, 43783350127, 43820680079, 43871224211): 877-882 failed + 43 errors per run, 909 node ids failing in all 5 and 918 in at least one (9 intermittent, all concurrency tests). The class-1 cascade (read-only `gitdir:` pointer, bug d724-6bb0-2674-42a0) is fixed on main; the remaining 918 ids sort into these classes by failure signature:\n\n| Class | Tests | Modules | Signature |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| max-path | 216 | 30 | `SnapshotError ... Filename too long`, `WinError 206` |\n| posix-shell | 143 | 23 | `bash` resolves to WSL with no distribution, `/bin/sh`, `.sh` scripts |\n| text-encoding | 133 | 58 | `UnicodeDecodeError` reading UTF-8 files with the cp1252 default |\n| posix-permissions | 47 | 8 | `0600 or stricter` key mode, `group/world accessible` artifact dir |\n| path-separators | 42 | 21 | `\\` vs `/` in asserted paths, cross-drive `relpath` |\n| posix-api | 28 | 16 | `fcntl`/`flock`, `signal.SIGKILL`, `DETACHED_PROCESS` stubs |\n| nested-pytest-plugins | 27 | 5 | nested pytest fails loading `pytest11` / root conftest plugin |\n| hardcoded-tmp | 21 | 5 | literal `/tmp/.ticket-sync-*` paths |\n| file-locks | 19 | 15 | `WinError 5`/`32` on open handles or read-only git objects, plus the 9 intermittent concurrency tests |\n| unclassified | 242 | 100 | assertion-level failures not yet root-caused |\n\nDecisions already recorded on this ticket (2026-10-26, user): narrow the advisory job to a maintained subset and hold that subset green; for MAX_PATH, shorten rebar's constructed paths and do not enable `core.longpaths` on the runner, because a runner setting hides the defect from CI while it stays live for downstream Windows users.\n\n## Approach\n\nHold a maintained subset green by deselecting the known-failing tests through pytest argument files, one file per defect class:\n\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/<class>.args`, each line `--deselect=<nodeid>` (or `--ignore=<module>` for `tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py`, which fails at collection). pytest's argument parser reads `@file` natively (`fromfile_prefix_chars=\"@\"`), so no conftest hook, plugin, env var or config key is added.\n- The `sweep (windows)` \"Run the default suite\" step passes every file as `'@.github/windows-sweep-deselect/<class>.args'`. The job stays `continue-on-error: true` (Windows is not a gate target), so a red sweep now means a NEW Windows regression.\n- The list is the union of the 5 runs above, so the 9 intermittent tests are covered.\n- `tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py` runs on the Linux gate and pins that every file is wired into the command and nothing else is, every line is a well-formed argument (sorted, unique, ASCII, LF only), no test sits in two classes, every listed module still exists, and every file carries the `eol=lf` git attribute.\n- `.gitattributes` pins `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/*.args` to `eol=lf`.\n- Each class becomes its own bug linked `discovered_from` this ticket. Fixing a class deletes its lines (and its file once empty), so the list only shrinks.\n\nRejected: comparing results against an enumerated baseline after the run. That needs a new junit-parsing script and CI step, and node ids are lossy in junit.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/workflows/test.yml` - pass the argument files to the Windows suite step and document the maintained-subset contract in the job comment. Landed in Gerrit 3402 (e0e55946d12).\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/*.args` (10 files) - the per-class deselect lists. Landed in 3402.\n- `tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py` - pins the files to the command. Landed in 3402; follow-up adds the LF byte check and the `git check-attr eol` check.\n- `.gitattributes` (follow-up) - `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/*.args eol=lf`.\n\nOut of scope: fixing any class (the child bugs own that), and making the job gate.\n\n## Follow-up after Gerrit 3402\n\nThe first `sweep (windows)` run on main after the merge (run 43975541557, job 133678433834) reported 1 failed, 19579 passed, 684 skipped. The failing test was `tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py::test_argfile_lines_are_well_formed_sorted_and_unique[posix-api.args]`, which saw the line `--ignore=tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py\\r`. The Windows checkout rewrote the `.args` files to CRLF, because `.gitattributes` has no rule for them. The `_LINE` regex let the trailing `\\r` through on `--deselect` lines (`(::.+)?` matches it) but rejected the one `--ignore` line, which must end in `.py`. Deselection itself still worked: argparse reads the file in text mode, and universal newlines strip the `\\r` (checked locally by parsing a CRLF argfile). The fix is the `eol=lf` attribute plus the two guard checks above.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py -q` passes (14 tests). Failure cases checked by hand: an unreferenced `.args` file, a malformed line, a line naming a missing module, a CRLF file, and removing the `eol=lf` attribute each make it fail.\n- `pytest --collect-only -m \"not integration and not external\" @.github/windows-sweep-deselect/*.args` on Linux collects without error. All 917 `--deselect` ids match a collected node id, so none is a silent no-op.\n- `make verify` green; `Verified +1` on Gerrit for each change.\n- After the follow-up merges: a `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` run whose `sweep (windows)` JOB (not only the workflow) concludes `success`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The 1626 failures and 1382 errors are classified into named defect classes with a count per class, so the work can be scoped and split.\n- [x] The `MAX_PATH` remedy is chosen explicitly between runner/Git long-path support and path shortening, with the tradeoff for downstream Windows consumers recorded.\n- [x] The `PermissionError` population is diagnosed rather than assumed — confirmed as file-handle lifetime, or identified as something else.\n- [x] A scoping decision is recorded: either Windows is supported to a readable-green standard, or the advisory job is narrowed to a maintained subset that is held green.\n- [x] After the change, `sweep (windows)` is in a state where a NEW regression would be visible — either green, or red with a known and enumerated baseline that CI compares against."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794988185944772991,"uuid":"23ffb63d-c8fc-45f6-9f8d-9db8d5d78e12"}